    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e1440285_a6b48d35",
        "filename": "CMakeLists.txt",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 417,
      "author": {
        "id": 3733880
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-22T02:57:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure if `__has_feature(bounds_attributes)` or `__has_feature(bounds_safety_attributes)` are ever true even if -fbounds-safety is not set. I think that would be the only case.\n\nOtherwise we can remove this variable entirely and trust that if the compiler advertises support, it\u0027s because its enabled and available",
      "parentUuid": "dd1e573c_c1271806",
      "revId": "6018b88715edc11413ce56e0902bb32c5bdd1e27",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fd203fff_530d8d1c",
        "filename": "CMakeLists.txt",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 417,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002219
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-22T20:54:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I\u0027m not sure if `__has_feature(bounds_attributes)` or `__has_feature(bounds_safety_attributes)` are ever true even if -fbounds-safety is not set. I think that would be the only case.\n\u003e \n\u003e Otherwise we can remove this variable entirely and trust that if the compiler advertises support, it\u0027s because its enabled and available\n\nLet\u0027s keep it simple for now and remove the flag. We already make the assumption that `__has_feature` is reliable with regard to sanitizers.",
      "parentUuid": "e1440285_a6b48d35",
      "revId": "6018b88715edc11413ce56e0902bb32c5bdd1e27",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
