      },
      "lineNbr": 417,
      "author": {
        "id": 3733880
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-23T21:11:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We can annotate functions x-module with _most_ annotations, except `__indexable` and `__bidi_indexable`. So we can use `__counted_by`, `__sized_by`, etc.\n\n\u003eDo we need an option or in the case where a header is included in multiple places you add the file level pragma to mark the file as unannotated and build them all with the bounds-safety flag?\n\nThis is an option I\u0027ve considered, but it felt like it was too much noise/churn on the codebase. I was assuming you\u0027d like this to be isolated to one place while we iterate. Enabling -fbounds-safety for all of libwebp would consist of:\n\n- Including src/util/bounds_safety.h in every file\n- Prepending WEBP_ASSUME_UNSAFE_INDEXABLE_ABI to all files\n- Replacing memcpy/memset/memmove with the macros provided in bounds_safety.h\n\nI\u0027m fine with this approach as well if you\u0027d prefer it :)",
      "parentUuid": "a7a5e022_c9477f03",
      "revId": "6018b88715edc11413ce56e0902bb32c5bdd1e27",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
